As of llvmorg-23.1.0, llvm-project's bazel overlay selects on
@llvm//platforms/config:{gnu,musl} to decide whether backtrace() and
mallinfo() are available. Those config settings come from the registry module
named "llvm", which declares bazel_compatibility >=7.7.0 -- newer than the
Bazel this repo pins in .bazelversion, and bumping that requires regenerating
the RBE toolchain configs (see the instructions in .bazelversion).

Drop the libc-flavour distinction instead. reclient builds against glibc on
Linux, so key the mallinfo define off the OS. A musl target would need this
revisited, as would adopting the registry module once Bazel is bumped.

--- a/utils/bazel/llvm-project-overlay/llvm/config.bzl
+++ b/utils/bazel/llvm-project-overlay/llvm/config.bzl
@@ -49,13 +49,12 @@
 backtrace_defines = select({
     "@platforms//os:windows": [],
-    "@llvm//platforms/config:musl": [],
     "//conditions:default": [
         "HAVE_BACKTRACE=1",
         "BACKTRACE_HEADER=<execinfo.h>",
     ],
 })

 mallinfo_defines = select({
-    "@llvm//platforms/config:gnu": ["HAVE_MALLINFO=1"],
+    "@platforms//os:linux": ["HAVE_MALLINFO=1"],
     "//conditions:default": [],
 })
